### Session 10 – Class Observations

- **Scaling AI products:** Scaling is not just about reaching more users; it is about consistently delivering the promised value and maintaining user trust.

- **Reliability and response time:** Delays or failures can have serious consequences. Just as timely responses are critical in healthcare, AI products must perform reliably when users need them.

- **Balancing trade-offs:** Product Managers must balance quality, latency and cost while making decisions that align with user expectations and business constraints.

- **Leadership and team support:** Effective leaders must make difficult decisions while protecting and supporting their teams.

- **Versioning and rollback:** Tracking model versions and changes helps teams identify performance issues and restore a previous reliable version when necessary.

- **Documentation and governance:** Maintaining records of decisions, changes and performance metrics supports accountability, auditability and continuous improvement. I could relate this to audit trails and quality management protocols in hospitals.

**Key takeaway:** Scaling AI products requires reliability, thoughtful trade-offs, strong team leadership and continuous monitoring. Documentation and version control are essential for maintaining trust, managing risks and improving performance over time.
